-- title:
--   The canonical projected atlas map obeys exact repointing covariance
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathbb Z^d$ act continuously on a topological space $X$. Fix natural scales $L_j\ge1$, an anisotropic clopen marker set, and continuous covariant marker-box data $B$ of comparison radius $S\ge24$. Let $D$ be support torsion data for a finite graph $H$, with positive exponent $k$, and put $m=2k+1$. Fix a height $K$, a coordinate $i$, a bound $J\ge0$, and one normalized carrier-contraction family for every positive width at most $6L_i$, with track bound $2(3m+8)(K+1)$ and joint bound $J$. Let $P_x:\mathbb R^d\to\mathcal S(H)$ be the canonical projected map obtained from these data at $x$. Then
--   $$P_x(z+t)=\tau^{\,t_i\bmod2}\bigl(P_{t\cdot x}(z)\bigr)
--   \qquad(x\in X,\ t\in\mathbb Z^d,\ z\in\mathbb R^d),$$
--   where $\mathcal S(H)$ is the compatible-probability-pair support space and $\tau$ swaps its shores.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (30 September 2026), Sections 2–7, supporting construction for Theorem 1.4 and Proposition 7.1; https://arxiv.org/html/2609.39824v1. Formalization-specific helper: AbelianTargets/CanonicalActionCovariance.lean, lines 81–110; SHA256 c8c0edd329c88d0a8523c9d49eecf1bb9a5a1c833f20443f8c80b33ad3a67d7b.

